### Live media updates — conditional-GET authz boundary (uc.memory.live-updates, cr-0107, ADR 0033)
# The unauthenticated boundary of the live-updates `listNodeMedia` (its new conditional-GET shape: an
# `If-None-Match` header + `since`/`sinceDelete` query params → a 304 or a keyset-delta 200 with both revisions
# and, on a delete, the current mediaId set). Runnable against ANY instance — no account/scope/membership needed.
# Like the media blob transport (en.memory.media) + cover.http, the authenticated happy-path is NOT reproducible
# from a bare .http: a 304 vs a 200-delta needs a member + scope + attached media (sealed client-side, PUT
# direct-to-store) plus the operator-blind grant flow. Those — the O(1) 304 short-circuit, the keyset delta past
# the cursor, the delete-reconcile id-set gated by delete_revision, the net-zero delete+add, and a cover change
# bumping neither counter — are covered at the integration layer (MediaSliceTest + NodeCoverSliceTest, which seed
# a member+scope in-tx and drive attach → poll → delete) and in the web client's live smoke.
#
# Run: ijhttp --env-file http/media/http-client.env.json --env dev http/media/live-updates.http

### 1. Poll listNodeMedia with an If-None-Match revision but NO bearer → generic 401 (auth before the conditional GET)
GET {{host}}/api/scopes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/nodes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/media
If-None-Match: 7

> {%
client.test("conditional GET still requires auth", function () {
    client.assert(response.status === 401, "expected 401, got " + response.status);
    client.assert(response.body.code === "authentication_failed", "expected authentication_failed");
});
%}

### 2. Poll with the keyset cursor + delete gate (since / sinceDelete) but NO bearer → 401 (the params don't bypass auth)
GET {{host}}/api/scopes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/nodes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/media?since=2026-07-09T12:34:56.789Z,00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000&sinceDelete=0

> {%
client.test("keyset-delta params still require auth", function () {
    client.assert(response.status === 401, "expected 401, got " + response.status);
    client.assert(response.body.code === "authentication_failed", "expected authentication_failed");
});
%}
